<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB AB Q1 EPS up to 0.92 crowns.</title>
<headline>ABB AB Q1 EPS up to 0.92 crowns.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG said first quarter net income per share of ABB AB, the Swedish holding company that owns half of the ABB Group, rose to 0.92 Swedish crowns from 0.79 crowns.</p>
<p>The ABB group said ABB AB's share of its group earnings before taxes rose six percent to $194 million, but after translating into Swedish crowns the rise amounted to 1,416 million crowns from 1,239 million.</p>
<p>ABB AB's net income rose 16 percent to 861 million crowns from 744 million.</p>
<p>Swedish ABB AB owns half of the ABB group and Swiss ABB AG owns the other half.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
